.TH PHYLLO-CHECK 1 "Phyllotaxis" "phyllo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phyllo-check \- validate a project's canonical Venation contract
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phyllo check
.RB [ --format
.BR text | json ]
.RB [ --quiet ]
.RB [ --scope
.BR venation ]
.br
.B phyllo check --help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phyllo check
discovers the nearest project root and installed Phyllotaxis package,
reads inert project configuration and canonical contract metadata, and
validates the Venation CSS contract. It does not change project files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --format text|json
Select human-readable text or the versioned JSON result. Text is the default.
JSON diagnostics are included in the result's diagnostics array.
.TP
.B --quiet
Suppress non-error human-readable success and informational output. Errors remain on
standard error. It does not alter the exit status.
.TP
.B --scope venation
Select the Venation validation scope. This is the only supported scope.
.TP
.B --help
Display command help on standard output without discovering a project.
.SH OUTPUT
In human mode, success is printed to standard output and errors to standard
error. With --format json, the required envelope includes schemaVersion, command,
ok, and diagnostics; paths, when present, are project-root-relative.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Validation completed with no violations.
.TP
.B 1
Validation completed with contract violations.
.TP
.B 2
Usage, configuration, or required package resolution error.
.TP
.B 3
Operational error prevented validation.
.TP
.B 4
Unexpected internal CLI failure.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT where the platform/runtime uses conventional signal propagation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phyllo (1)
.br
docs/cli/phyllo.md in the source repository documents the canonical command contract.
